    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01dc6e6f_94da7612",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/include/usbc/tcpc_generic_emul.h",
        "patchSetId": 39
      },
      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-03T20:21:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is needed.  The tests have been updated to use `irq-gpios`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "7c8e6df9dd635a730e8c391037a6545e6c9de037",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "00baa45f_f64bb4d0",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/include/usbc/tcpc_generic_emul.h",
        "patchSetId": 39
      },
      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 1548775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-03T21:53:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The emulator has been updated to use `irq-gpios` in all situations, but testing the tcpc interrupt still requires the `tcpc_config` to use `int-pin` when the legacy interrupt is being used.\n\nI temporarily considered changing the emulator to use `int-pin` when `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_TCPC_INTERRUPT\u003dn`, but thought better of it since that would make the macros way too complicated just for a insignificant sense of consistency. So now when testing `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_TCPC_INTERRUPT\u003dn`, the `tcpc_port` has both `irq-gpios` and `int-pin` properties. The emulator is initialized from the `irq-gpios` and the `tcpc_config` and interrupt is initialized from `int-pin`.",
